{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and a leader of the County of Tripoli a Crusader state in the Holy Land. He was born in 1140 and died in 1187. Raymond was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His mother was the daughter of Baldwin II King of Jerusalem.\n\n*Early Life and Regency* \nRaymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli at a young age after his father's assassination in 1152. As he was a minor a regency was established with his mother Hodierna acting as regent. However Hodierna's regency was short-lived as she was soon forced to return to Jerusalem due to a dispute with her sister Melisende. The regency then passed to Amalric Count of Jaffa who later became King Amalric of Jerusalem.\n\nRaymond III came of age in 1155 and began to rule Tripoli in his own right. He was a capable leader and worked to strengthen his county. In 1160 he was captured by Nur ad-Din Zangi the ruler of Aleppo and Damascus. He was released in 1164 after paying a ransom and being exchanged for hostages.\n\n*Marriage and Alliances* \nIn 1160s Raymond III married Eschiva of Bures the widow of Walter of Saint Omer the Prince of Galilee. The marriage helped to secure an alliance between Tripoli and the Principality of Galilee. Raymond III also formed an alliance with Bohemond III of Antioch and together they fought against the forces of Nur ad-Din Zangi.\n\n*The Battle of Hattin and Death* \nIn 1187 Raymond III played a key role in the events leading up to the Battle of Hattin. He was initially opposed to the plan to launch a campaign against Saladin but eventually agreed to join the army led by Guy of Lusignan. The Crusader army was defeated at Hattin and Raymond III was one of the few leaders who escaped. He died soon after the battle possibly due to injuries sustained during the fighting. Raymond III was succeeded by his godson Raymond IV who was the son of Bohemond III of Antioch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.011065074242651463}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0003358753747306764}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.7881377516459906e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0016014858847483993}, {"token": " nob", "logprob": -0.19904756546020508}, {"token": "leman", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.019826099276542664}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.6682716608047485}, {"token": " leader", "logprob": -0.33231237530708313}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0019388464279472828}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " County", "logprob": -0.7008846998214722}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.06233595684170723}, {"token": " Crus", "logprob": -0.07892731577157974}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " state", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.31618574261665344}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0016683719586580992}, {"token": " Holy", "logprob": -0.127301886677742}, {"token": " Land", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.00455532455816865}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.0006767605082131922}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.0005683475756086409}, {"token": " born", "logprob": -0.03029482252895832}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.6931542158126831}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.20168423652648926}, {"token": "114", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.006716059520840645}, {"token": " died", "logprob": -0.8335854411125183}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -5.829164365422912e-05}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -5.96046277